::ENG2_U05_L06_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Ideas: Some students ride late buses. They need a place to study. Which revision best connects the ideas?{
=A. Because some students ride late buses, they need a place to study after school.#Correct. Because correctly shows the reason relationship.
~B. However, some students ride late buses, they need a place to study.#Incorrect. However signals contrast and the sentence is awkward.
~C. Some students ride late buses, they need a place to study.#Incorrect. This is a comma splice.
~D. Students buses study because late.#Incorrect. This is unclear.
}

::ENG2_U05_L06_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which transition best shows result?{
~A. However#Incorrect. However shows contrast.
=B. As a result#Correct. As a result signals an effect.
~C. For example#Incorrect. For example introduces an example.
~D. In addition#Incorrect. In addition adds another idea.
}

::ENG2_U05_L06_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which sentence is correctly joined?{
~A. The library closes early, students work in hallways.#Incorrect. This is a comma splice.
~B. The library closes early students work in hallways.#Incorrect. This is a run-on.
=C. The library closes early; as a result, students sometimes work in hallways.#Correct. The semicolon and transition correctly join related complete thoughts.
~D. Because the library closes early.#Incorrect. This is a fragment.
}

::ENG2_U05_L06_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG2.V.03] Which transition creates the most precise relationship? Sentence: "The library has limited staff; _____, students still need a supervised place after school."{
~A. therefore#Incorrect. Therefore signals result, but the sentence needs contrast.
~B. in addition#Incorrect. This signals addition.
~C. for example#Incorrect. This signals an example.
=D. however#Correct. However shows contrast between limited staff and student need.
}

::ENG2_U05_L06_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which revision best improves cohesion?{
~A. The library closes. Students wait. Hallways loud.#Incorrect. This is choppy and unclear.
=B. Because the library closes before late buses depart, some students wait in loud hallways instead of a quiet study space.#Correct. This connects ideas clearly for the audience.
~C. Library closes buses wait good.#Incorrect. This is unclear.
~D. However therefore because library.#Incorrect. Random transitions do not create cohesion.
}
